{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix pushed for review as change 2988\n\n`d31375d26a9` — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2988\n\n**Scope held to the 3 files in `file_impact`:**\n\n```\n infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md   |  41 +++++++\n infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh    |  50 ++++++++-\n tests/infra/test_mcp_entrypoint.py | 211 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n```\n\n**What changed.** `provision_code()` no longer returns early for any present checkout. A clean workspace now fetches `origin main` and fast-forwards under the same directory lock the clone path already used. Dirty, diverged, and unreachable-remote states refuse and return non-zero without touching the workspace. Missing or unresolvable-HEAD checkouts still re-clone as before. Each refresh logs the HEAD SHA and the ahead/behind distance from `origin/main`, before and after.\n\n**Startup behaviour on a refusal.** `provision_code` failure sets `rc=1` on `provision_store`, which normal startup backgrounds, so a dirty volume logs loudly and the server still starts. The refusal makes the stale tree visible rather than wedging the container — which matters, because wedging would convert this bug into an outage.\n\n**TDD evidence.** The required first test failed for the right reason before any production change:\n\n```\n>       assert _head(checkout) == remote_tip, result.stderr\nE       AssertionError: assert 'cbf508d29622...' == 'bf003333e76a...'\n```\n\nAll 8 tests were mutation-checked and each one killed its mutant. `make lint` green, including actionlint.\n\nNot yet voted. AC verification waits on the change landing and on a subsequent gate run reading a fresh tree."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789788884966378434,"uuid":"6baaca9c-d157-4969-912d-7e9716ae65a5"}